{{Codex|This intelligent hammer takes an enemy killed by a Heavy Attack and recomposes them as an ally. Any fatal strike with this weapon also performs a Codex scan.}}
'''Synoid Heliocor''' is the [[Syndicate]] variant of the {{Weapon|Heliocor}}, unique to {{Faction|Cephalon Suda}}, sporting improved [[status chance]] and attack speed at the expense of [[critical chance]]. It also has the ability to scan targets it kills into the [[Codex]] (including a chance to award [[Kavat Genetic Code]] for killing [[Feral Kavat]]s, but it is unable to award any [[Cephalon Simaris]] standing), with completed entries generating a friendly [[Specter]] of an enemy it kills with a [[Heavy Attack]].

This weapon can be sold for {{cc|5,000}}

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals primarily {{D|Impact}} damage.
*Enemy kills with this weapon are scanned and registered into the [[Codex]] (but will not award any [[Cephalon Simaris]] standing).
*Able to award [[Kavat Genetic Code]] when killing [[Feral Kavat]]s in [[Orokin Derelict]] missions.
*[[Heavy Attack]] kills creates a [[Specter]] of the killed enemy for '''30''' seconds if that enemy's Codex entry is completed. Only one specter can be created at a time.
*Stance slot has {{Pol|Madurai}} polarity, matches {{M|Crushing Ruin}} stance.

{{Advantages|
*Tied with {{Weapon|Heliocor}} for the second highest base damage of all hammers, behind {{Weapon|Arca Titron}}.
*Highest [[status chance]] of all hammers.
*Second fastest [[attack speed]] of all hammers, behind {{Weapon|Volnus}}.
*Has an initial [[Melee|Combo Count]] of 20 (2.0x heavy attack multiplier).
}}

{{Disadvantages|
}}

